row(7, 89, 'MATERIAL', f'THE VOICE SPEAKING ITSELF — BY THE POINTS. "{H(7, 89, "ובבא", "משה", "אל", "אהל", "מועד", "לדבר", "אתו")}" ("and when Moses came into the tent of meeting to speak with Him"), "{H(7, 89, "וישמע", "את", "הקול", "מדבר", "אליו")}" ("he heard the Voice speaking to him") — מִדַּבֵּר ("speaking itself", the reflexive stem with its tav swallowed: a hiriq under the mem, a dagesh — the doubling dot — in the dalet) at {len(MID_REFLEX)} Tanakh seats ({", ".join(MID_REFLEX)}) against מְדַבֵּר ("speaking", the active) at {MID_PIEL} and מִדְבָּר ("wilderness") at {MID_WILD} — one consonantal word, three words by the points (computed on the DB\'s own marks; sitting 1b\'s law at a verb); "{H(7, 89, "מעל", "הכפרת", "אשר", "על", "ארן", "העדת")}" ("from above the cover that is on the ark of the testimony"), "{H(7, 89, "מבין", "שני", "הכרבים")}" ("from between the two cherubim") — Exod 25:22\'s phrase, its two seats (computed); Lev 1:1\'s "from the tent of meeting" the third of the Sifrei\'s three — two verses contradicting, "let them stand in their place until a third comes and reconciles" — the thirteenth rule of Rabbi Ishmael on this verse (piska 58 row 1); "{H(7, 89, "וידבר", "אליו")}" ("and He spoke to him") — the DB\'s plain narrative-past, the active stem (computed) → {A(7, 89, "וכד", "עליל", "משה", "למשכן", "זמנא", "למללא", "עמיה")} ("and WHENEVER Moses entered the tent of meeting to speak with Him"), {A(7, 89, "ושמע", "ית", "קלא", "דמתמלל", "עמיה")} ("he heard the voice SPEAKING ITSELF with him") and {A(7, 89, "ומתמלל", "עמיה")} ("and it was speaking itself with him") — the translation reads the entry as habitual and BOTH verbs as the Voice\'s self-speech, the reflexive a second time where the Hebrew has the active; the Sifrei\'s thirteen utterances to Moses alone, Aaron excluded (piska 58 row 1), and the great voice against the still small one (row 2).')
